$DATUM General procedure V: synthesis of intermediates 17a-d To a stirred
suspension of the carboxylic acid derivative (1 eq) in DCM (2 mL / mmol
carboxylic acid), TBTU (1.1 eq) and N,N-diisopropylethylamine (2 eq) were
added, followed by the corresponding amine (1 eq). The clear solution was
stirred at room temperature until either TLC or HPLC confirmed complete
conversion. The occurring precipitate was collected by filtration, washed
with DCM and purified by silica flash-chromatography.
4-Bromo-N-cyclopropylbenzamide (17a) 17a was synthesized according to
general procedure V. Eluent: ethyl acetate/n-hexane 80/20 → ethyl
acetate/n-hexane 50/50 afforded 89 % yield as a white solid. 1H NMR (200
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.50 (s, 1H), 7.40 (s, 4H), 1.60-1.36 (m, 1H), 1.15-1.01
(m, 2H), 0.93-0.76 (m, 2H). FAB-MS (m/z): 240/242 [M+H]+.
